    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule for `POST /api/owners`: creating an owner is now rejected with **409 Conflict** when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners.\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern (not Spring MVC controllers), I added:\n\n1. **`ValidateCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a read-only validation gate that counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitively, matching `BuildOwner`'s existing count logic) and throws `CityAtCapacityException` when the count is \u2265 50. It publishes nothing and only escalates on conflict.\n\n2. **`CityAtCapacityException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception so it appears in the `throws` clause.\n\n3. **`CityAtCapacityExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT`, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneExceptionHandler`.\n\n4. **Escalation YAML** \u2014 `org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.CityAtCapacityException.yml` wiring the exception to its handler.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** \u2014 inserted a `cityCapacity` step into `owners.POST.yml` after the household gate and before `applyHousehold`, so the rejection happens before any entity is built or persisted (consistent with the other validation gates).\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` passes, and the full suite is green.",
