    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive extension that matches the established conventions of this codebase.\n\n- `ValidateCityCapacity` is a near-perfect structural mirror of the existing sibling validators. It follows `ValidateUniqueTelephone` exactly: `service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)`, a read-only gate that scans `ownerRepository.findAll()` and throws a checked escalation on conflict, publishing nothing. The `for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll())` scan is the already-established idiom here, not a new smell \u2014 so the duplication question resolves in favor of consistency.\n- Naming (`Validate<X>`), the one-public-method rule, the checked-exception-extends-`Exception` requirement, and the escalation handler + YAML placement all conform to AGENTS.md and to the neighboring files.\n- Pipeline wiring is correct and well-placed: slotted between `uniqueHousehold` and `applyHousehold`, keeping it with the other read-only validation gates *before* anything is built or persisted, matching the stated intent and the comment conventions of the other steps.\n- Responsibilities are well-partitioned across the three new units (exception / handler / function); nothing is becoming a catch-all, and the constant `CITY_CAPACITY` is sensibly localized to the gate that enforces it.\n\nA maintainer of this repo would find this entirely natural.",
